    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05487277_cc8d9ee7",
        "filename": "driver/charger/bq24773.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 226,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-12-11T01:59:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The charge inhibit bit is only set by a charger_set_mode(CHARGE_FLAG_INHIBIT_CHARGE), which is only set by charge state machine when we don\u0027t want to charge (desired voltage \u003d desired current \u003d 0). A sysjump should cause this bit to get reset and the charge state machine will re-determine what it wants to charge at when it first runs.\n\nIn terms of charging from a dual-role device, that is done by setting the charge_en GPIO. Since gpio\u0027s don\u0027t change on a sysjump, there will be no immediate change. After the sysjump, things should work as expected: PD state machine will detect charger and notify charge_manager which will set active charge port only once we confirm port partner is not a dual-role device.",
      "parentUuid": "454eea83_9a52395b",
